<title>GERMANY: EAST GERMAN APRIL INDUSTRY ORDERS RISE 4.0 PCT M/M.</title>
<headline>EAST GERMAN APRIL INDUSTRY ORDERS RISE 4.0 PCT M/M.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS     Apr 97     Mar 97     Apr 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   +4.0	 +4.1	 +2.7</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +21.1	+19.5	 -2.8</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		151.8	145.9	125.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted, provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details (mth-on-mth)</p>
<p>				  Apr 97    Mar 97    Apr 97 index</p>
<p> Domestic orders	     +4.3	-0.1	162.9</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Mar/Apr 97 with Jan/Feb 97:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		  +9.0</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Mar/Apr 97 with Mar/Apr 96:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		 +17.2</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 +8.3</p>
<p> Foreign orders			 +61.0</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		   +13.7</p>
<p> Capital goods			  +28.4</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    +2.8</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
